{"kind":"request","text":"S2: deliver checkout creation, its advisory record and lane refs.\n\nThis is a stage child of #22168, governed by Hugh's effective adoption ba18cd1a of proposal 7a71886b and the exact 3f817c3b design. The signed attachments preserve that adopted text. It is ordinary proposal adoption, not an inferred authority-bearing research request. All ten adopted differences govern. Ordinary inherited staleness stays visible; the historical decision and parent are not silently replaced. Current source reconciliation starts at main 359b211c, including its receipt-discharge fix and fold profile24. Claude confirmed stage scope and availability in #22308.\n\nDelivery order is S1, S2, then S3. Keep #22093's implementation/review handoff ahead of substantive lane work; use its genuine review waits and keep ready independent reviews moving. Each stage has its own promise, exact reporting artifacts, independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, requester ratification, sealed exact-path succession, source/sequence/receipt push, main CI and owned checkout/branch cleanup. Attribute fresh tests and carried evidence accurately. Docs rest on their behavior artifacts and every cited source file has a working exact-head preview. Exercise the adopted real-Git fixtures and meaningful omissions for the boundaries this stage changes, plus the applicable normal Go, vet, race, UI and docset gates. No new broad test framework or gratuitous repeated whole-suite execution.\n\nThe parent owes all three stages. S1 and S2 artifacts report their child commitments only; their landings must not close the full parent promise. Before the final S3 review, account for all three outcomes and plan its exact-head reporting/review scope so the complete parent can close through the ordinary guarded landing mechanism only after all conditions are met. Do not manufacture a design-only completion or a second closure for one commitment. No live existing-tree cleanup, live hook install